patrone-notepad (0.3.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Patrone's own header bar: the side panel's button, the tabs as pills
    (the selected one in Patrone Blue), a new tab button, command search
    and Settings; the File, Edit and View menus, with the same items and
    keys, in a slim row under it.
  * A side panel (View, F9): the window's open tabs, recent files, and a
    Markdown file's outline, its headings, to go to one.
  * Command search (Ctrl+K): type a few words ("word wrap", "line endings
    crlf", "go to line") and run the command they find. Link moves to
    Ctrl+Shift+K.
  * The status bar: a zoom slider (its percentage resets it), and a
    Markdown file's words and reading time, beside the line endings' and
    encoding's menus.
  * A Markdown file's preview beside it (Ctrl+Alt+P, the formatting bar's
    Preview), formatted throughout and scrolling with the text.
  * Version history (File, a tab's right click): a version of each file,
    and each note not saved yet, every few minutes while it changes, when
    it's saved, and when its changes are closed without saving, to look
    at and restore (Undo takes a restore back). Each keeps its newest 50,
    none older than 30 days, under 100 MB in all, in
    ~/.local/state/patrone-notepad/history. Only while Restore open tabs
    (auto-save) is on; turning it off deletes them.
  * Line numbers and a shaded current line (View, or Settings); pinned
    tabs (a tab's right click), which stay at the start and aren't closed
    by a middle click or Close other tabs; and a new note named after its
    first line, which Save as suggests as its file name.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 16:00:00 -0600

patrone-notepad (0.2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Markdown: .md files show formatted while they're edited. Headings,
    bold, italic, strikethrough, inline code, links (Ctrl+click opens
    them), bulleted, numbered and task lists (their boxes can be ticked),
    quotes, code blocks, tables, rules and images (from files, by their
    path or beside the document) show as they'd look, with the markup
    hidden except on the lines being edited. The text itself doesn't
    change: opening and saving a file leaves it exactly as it was.
  * A formatting bar under the menus for Markdown files: the line's heading
    level (Ctrl+Alt+1 to 6, Ctrl+Alt+0 for text), bold (Ctrl+B), italic
    (Ctrl+I), strikethrough (Ctrl+Shift+X), bulleted (Ctrl+Shift+8) and
    numbered (Ctrl+Shift+7) lists, link (Ctrl+K), clear formatting
    (Ctrl+\), and an outline of the headings to go to one.
  * View › Formatted Markdown, and a switch in the status bar (Ctrl+Shift+M),
    show a Markdown file as typed instead; Settings › Markdown formatting
    turns it off for every file. File › Export as HTML saves a Markdown
    file as a web page.
  * PatroneOS's fonts by name: PatroneOS Sans for the app's own words and
    formatted Markdown, PatroneOS Mono for plain text and code. The font
    list starts with the five PatroneOS families. Depends on
    fonts-patroneos, which it recommended before.
  * Markdown files (text/markdown) open in Notepad.
  * Save with nothing changed leaves the file alone.
  * Settings › About and licences: Notepad's licence, what it's built
    with and their licences, and the full texts of its Rust crates'
    (third-party-licenses.txt.gz). The copyright file names every licence:
    the crates' (MIT, Apache-2.0, the Unlicense, Unicode-3.0), GTK's and
    its libraries' (from their own packages) and the fonts' (OFL).

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0600

patrone-notepad (0.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * First package: Notepad, a plain text editor with tabs across the title
    bar and a + button for a new one; File, Edit and View menus with
    Settings at the end of their row; and a status bar with the cursor's
    line and column, the number of characters (and how many are selected),
    the zoom, the line endings and the encoding, the last two of which can
    be changed from there.
  * New tab, New window, Open, Save, Save as, Save all, Print, Close tab,
    Close window and Exit; Undo, Redo, Cut, Copy, Paste, Delete, Find, Find
    next and previous, Replace, Go to line, Select all, the time and date,
    and Font; Zoom, the status bar and word wrap.
  * Find and replace in a box over the text, finding as you type, with
    Match case and Wrap around.
  * Reads UTF-8 (with or without a byte order mark), UTF-16 and CP1252
    text, with LF, CRLF or CR line endings, and saves it the same way.
  * Settings: the app's theme (light, dark or the desktop's), the font
    (PatroneOS Mono, 11 points, by default), word wrap, whether files from
    other apps open in a new tab or a new window, and whether to restore
    open tabs: on, Notepad keeps the open tabs and their unsaved changes as
    you work (in ~/.local/state/patrone-notepad), without changing the
    files, and brings them back when it starts; off, it starts with a new
    tab and asks to save changes when it closes.
  * The notepad command, its launcher entry and Patrone's own icon. Files
    can be dropped on the window to open them.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0600
